        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Southern Africa, Zimbabwe, Zambia, Zambezi River\n- Concepts: British protectorates, national borders, founding\n- People: Cecil Rhodes\n- Organizations: Groote Schuur Zoo\n\nFacts:\n- The former British protectorate in southern Africa was divided into two countries separated by the Zambezi River.\n- Zimbabwe lies south of the Zambezi River, and Zambia lies north of the river.\n- Cecil Rhodes founded the former British protectorate.\n- Cecil Rhodes also established the Groote Schuur Zoo in 1975.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "71c4d809-58b2-54ed-a403-a716a475f84a",
        "text": "The former British protectorate of the southern Africa territory became two countries with the Zambezi river as the border. Zimbabwe lies to the south; Zambia is north of the river. It was founded by the man who established the Groote Schuur Zoo in 1975.",
